t one time  having paper reports wheeled in on a  cart wasn't doing anything there were  lots of problems that were masked we had  to focus on the right issues there were  so many things that we had to do  so this think differently act  courageously became our motto and what  did it change they're calling the Dallas  miracle and for decades Dallas they  measure school districts in quartiles  and generally Dallas ISD has been in the  third quartile never moved out of it for  decades and in one year we popped into  the top of the second quartile that and  it's a result of lots of changes that  were supported by data and this is a  different way to look at it different  metrics that they're tracking going down  as a good thing so entering this year  this is my third school year entering  this year  we have some interesting and very  promising results we have 300 million  dollars in the bank it's a big deal now  our school district isn't operating in  the red if something happened and  funding stopped our school district  could continue to operate for three to  four months in the past on the first day  of school there were an enormous number  of vacancies teacher vacancies in the  classroom  in 2012 there 860 on the first day out  of nine 9600 teachers this year we only  had 14 huge change all of our kids eat  for free the at 90 percent free and  reduced lunch it was actually cheaper  for us just to feed them all for free  than collect money for that other 10%  there are lots of other accomplishments  that we have backed by data we took our  principals to performance pay and now  it's tied to their their compensation is  tied to their performance our teacher  excellence initiative which does the  same thing it takes teachers off of  tenure and puts them on performance pay  that was passed by our board in the  spring and it started this school year  we have you know Obama challenged  schools to speed up the internet so that  we could have communication speeds in  the classroom that were high and we did  that but we did 20 gigabytes the  classroom because we believe that  personalized learning is where our  districts going by 2020 we're going to  open four to eight personalized learning  schools next school year so this is very  important to us the other thing was  fence defense it was really important  that kids could not be inside the school  but near the school and get access to  the Internet in many of our poor  neighborhoods the kids don't have a  device they don't go home to a computer  and Internet  so we began in one of our initiatives a  one-to-one device where we sent it where  we're going to send a home with the kids  we also installed Wireless paid for by D  is d and a lot of high density housing  and then destination 2020 is our  strategic plan and we now have all these  benchmark data and we can actually  measure and I know that sounds like  they're not what you should do but it  wasn't available this is what our  teacher excellence initiative looks like  every kind of teacher has different ways  they need to be evaluated so this pie  chart looks different across the board  fifty percent is based on spot  observations how do you how do you  handle your classroom what is your  classroom management style are you  prepared so 10 spot observations or  formal observations 50 percent 15  percent based on student surveys that  was proven out through some scientific  research and then this rest of it is  based on student achievement but many  different metrics so not heavily  weighted to the state exams or the AP  exam but a mixture of things the other  thing it's really interesting is working  to pull the pay out so that our best  teachers can make a lot more money and I  think that's really important in  acquiring new people into our field and  to encourage the kind of professionalism  that we want so this year we're going to  focus a lot more on insights I showed  you a little bit of that this  personalized learning that's going to be  really important in it a lot of the back  end of what we do has to change you  think about schools it's all based on  semesters scheduling at a semester but  he said Algebra one has to take exactly  two semesters so we want to loosen up  the timeframe and allow kids to take as  long as they need to complete classes  one of the things we spend a lot of time  working on is equitable access  there's definitely not equitable access  to our bus teachers our best teachers  are in those magnet schools that are the  best in the country and we've got to  really work on how do we ensure that all  of our kids have an effective awesome  teacher teaching their class counselor  evaluations counselors are working with  our children on social emotional issues  but they're also the ones that counsel  them on what classes they should enroll  in evaluating those rigorously is going  to be very important coaching holding  our coaches get extra mentor for  coaching we need to hold them  accountable for what they're doing in  the past it's been you know okay you're  a coach and there was not a lot of  oversight we're taking our human  resources and our finance dashboards and  really diving deep so that we understand  lots of things that in past we haven't  even begun to think about this is what  personalized learning looks like to me  we think about all of these back-end  systems that I have to glue together and  all of these places where it's very  rigged it's very rigid maybe in time  that we have to bust through all of that  and so I spend a lot of my time thinking  about how we're going to take all of the  different things that we have and glue  them together to offer an awesome  education that's personalized to the  child based on where they are and I  think this is kind of the next great  step that we have to make and a lot of  the things that I think about is there's  so many curriculum on how to teach  photosynthesis and we know that possibly  that photosynthesis exercise works  really well with this type of kids but  not this type of kids you know think of  ranking that's pervasive in that other  industries we're gonna have to get good  at that  so I hope you'll all watch us as we  continue down our very brave and bold  path as we work to improve education in  Dallas
 

